// relay.proto — smind relay wire contract (daemon ↔ relay, ADR-0007 (f)).
//
// The relay is a dumb pipe: it authenticates connections (ADR-0011) and
// forwards opaque ciphertext frames between a daemon and its paired mobile
// devices. It never sees an E2EE session key and cannot inspect Frame
// payloads.
//
// Control/data socket mapping (ADR-0007 (b), decided here as the ADR left
// it to this plan):
//
//   - Control socket  -> OpenControl, one bidi stream per daemon↔relay
//     connection. It owns connection/session lifecycle: device attach and
//     detach announcements, liveness, and (later) buffer/ack bookkeeping.
//     It carries no application payload.
//   - Data socket     -> OpenData, one bidi stream per paired device per
//     E2EE session — opened by the daemon for each device and by the mobile
//     device itself, so fanout is "one stream per device" rather than a
//     shared pipe needing multiplexing. Each Frame is a self-contained
//     envelope (routing metadata + opaque ciphertext), which is also what
//     the reconnect buffer (ADR-0007 (a)) stores and flushes on reconnect.
//
// A single multiplexed stream carrying a tagged envelope for both control
// and data was considered and rejected: it reintroduces exactly the ad hoc
// multiplexing the control/data split exists to avoid, and control liveness
// would then share flow control with bulk ciphertext.
//
// Relay admission (ADR-0011) is deliberately unary and separate from both
// streams: AdmitChallenge issues a server nonce, then Admit carries the
// daemon's SCRAM-style proof over the transcript (protocol version,
// relay host id, both nonces, daemon key ID). The raw relay host secret never
// appears on the wire, and the hash the relay stores is not sufficient to
// forge the proof. A connection is bound to one relay host; Frames whose
// relay host or session ID mismatch the binding are rejected by the relay
// implementation (not the wire contract). Admission is independent of the E2EE handshake,
// which happens inside the encrypted payload the relay forwards blindly.

